(3053002, 430235, 67324, '<td valign="top">Nice and sharp detail. I think i prefer the balance to be reversed, i.e more sky, less track</td>', 'Nice and sharp detail. I think i prefer the balance to be reversed, i.e more sky, less track', '2006-11-22 01:54:00.000000', NULL, 1),
(3053006, 428119, 52130, '<td valign="top">her eyes look very cartoony, almost fake. Not really a bad thing, just looks that way to me.</td>', 'her eyes look very cartoony, almost fake. Not really a bad thing, just looks that way to me.', '2006-11-22 01:55:01.000000', NULL, 1),
(3053011, 429816, 52130, '<td valign="top">different composition, but otherwise uninteresting</td>', 'different composition, but otherwise uninteresting', '2006-11-22 01:56:28.000000', NULL, 1),
(3053013, 429844, 16241, '<td valign="top">nice one, dont think the paper on bench adds to this great photo.</td>', 'nice one, dont think the paper on bench adds to this great photo.', '2006-11-22 01:56:54.000000', NULL, 1),
(3053015, 429993, 16241, '<td valign="top">lovely photo.  fresh, clear, happy.</td>', 'lovely photo.  fresh, clear, happy.', '2006-11-22 01:57:30.000000', NULL, 1),
(3053017, 430435, 67324, '<td valign="top">I like it. If it was artificially warmer (tweaked white balance)and the road was leading straight into the horizon, or shot higher such that the yellow lines continued into the image unbroken I would prefer it more.</td>', 'I like it. If it was artificially warmer (tweaked white balance)and the road was leading straight into the horizon, or shot higher such that the yellow lines continued into the image unbroken I would prefer it more.', '2006-11-22 01:57:36.000000', NULL, 1),
(3053018, 429908, 29269, '<td valign="top">Is there a reason for mixing figures this way? It immediately caught my attention, and I cannot decide if it has some hidden meaning, if it is supposed to enhance the artistic impression, or if it is just an oversight. I''m leaning towards the oversight theory, as it bothers me for some reason.</td>', 'Is there a reason for mixing figures this way? It immediately caught my attention, and I cannot decide if it has some hidden meaning, if it is supposed to enhance the artistic impression, or if it is just an oversight. I''m leaning towards the oversight theory, as it bothers me for some reason.', '2006-11-22 01:57:40.000000', NULL, 1),
(3053021, 428436, 67324, '<td valign="top">More detail up the top would be ace. Good subject.</td>', 'More detail up the top would be ace. Good subject.', '2006-11-22 01:58:25.000000', NULL, 1),
(3053029, 430246, 51660, '<td valign="top">I like this a lot. If I am to offer any critique, then I would have liked it better if the farmers hat did not run in with the gate like it does.</td>', 'I like this a lot. If I am to offer any critique, then I would have liked it better if the farmers hat did not run in with the gate like it does.', '2006-11-22 01:59:47.000000', NULL, 1),
