(3070155, 429144, 51660, '<td valign="top">Thanks to everybody who voted for this one. This was my first entry in a challenge and I am very happy placing this high on the list.<br/> <br/>Several people have asked where it is taken and what I am doing here. I am providing engineering support for a science team studying the Weddell seal population at Ross Island in Antarctica. We are 7 people in a small camp on the sea ice off the coast. Looking at a globe, go South from New Zealand and you get to the Ross Sea and Ross Island. This is where many of the old explorers were a long time ago and both Scott''s and Shackelton''s huts are just a few miles from our camp.<br/>We often have Adelie Penguins around but this was a rare visit by Emperors.<br/> <br/>If you are interested in seeing more pictures or reading more about this then please visit my website at: <a href="//www.viking-photography.com" rel="nofollow" target="_blank">//www.viking-photography.com</a><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-11-29 00:54:24.</i></td>', 'Thanks to everybody who voted for this one. This was my first entry in a challenge and I am very happy placing this high on the list. Several people have asked where it is taken and what I am doing here. I am providing engineering support for a science team studying the Weddell seal population at Ross Island in Antarctica. We are 7 people in a small camp on the sea ice off the coast. Looking at a globe, go South from New Zealand and you get to the Ross Sea and Ross Island. This is where many of the old explorers were a long time ago and both Scott''s and Shackelton''s huts are just a few miles from our camp.We often have Adelie Penguins around but this was a rare visit by Emperors. If you are interested in seeing more pictures or reading more about this then please visit my website at: //www.viking-photography.com', '2006-11-29 00:51:25.000000', '2006-11-29 00:54:24.000000', 0),
