(3070700, 429397, 52549, '<td valign="top">Hi Kelly,<br/>Strangely enough (or perhaps not strangely enough) I can understand your reasons perfectly - and I definitely understand the need sometimes to do something "different", which is always a risky thing to do here.<br/>Your shot can do do well - or not...<br/>One thing''s for sure - I stared at your shot for the longest time trying to work out why. It''s great that you took the time to explain.<br/></td>', 'Hi Kelly,Strangely enough (or perhaps not strangely enough) I can understand your reasons perfectly - and I definitely understand the need sometimes to do something "different", which is always a risky thing to do here.Your shot can do do well - or not...One thing''s for sure - I stared at your shot for the longest time trying to work out why. It''s great that you took the time to explain.', '2006-11-29 04:27:25.000000', NULL, 0),
(3070709, 428767, 33352, '<td valign="top">Good finish Shez, well deserved.</td>', 'Good finish Shez, well deserved.', '2006-11-29 04:36:03.000000', NULL, 0),
(3070712, 428662, 66923, '<td valign="top">Thank you all very much for your comments. I thought this would make it in top 20, but I am happy with 22nd place. I am quite new at posting (this being only my second challenge) and I can see that my borders are lowering my score. I entered a decent shot in the Diagonal challenge as well, and I already got comments on my borders being too large. <br/> <br/> The thing is i like my borders, I feel they help concentrating over the picture itself, they bring the viewer closer. thats how i like it and i am not gonna change it just to get extra points here. If u like my pics, but hate the borders, well then, I will live with that, and, at the end of the challenge I will pretend I have a bit of a higher score.<br/> <br/> Thanks again for the comments. And, Kelly, I would be happy to send you a large version of this shot, so u can print it and put it on your wall. Thanks again!</td>', 'Thank you all very much for your comments. I thought this would make it in top 20, but I am happy with 22nd place. I am quite new at posting (this being only my second challenge) and I can see that my borders are lowering my score. I entered a decent shot in the Diagonal challenge as well, and I already got comments on my borders being too large.   The thing is i like my borders, I feel they help concentrating over the picture itself, they bring the viewer closer. thats how i like it and i am not gonna change it just to get extra points here. If u like my pics, but hate the borders, well then, I will live with that, and, at the end of the challenge I will pretend I have a bit of a higher score.  Thanks again for the comments. And, Kelly, I would be happy to send you a large version of this shot, so u can print it and put it on your wall. Thanks again!', '2006-11-29 04:37:55.000000', NULL, 0),
(3070727, 430100, 31133, '<td valign="top">Very pretty lighting... so golden! I would love to visit Jordan someday. You''ve shown me such a beautiful place. Might be nice to see the boy in front of one of the pillars so he stands out a little more, but I''m really glad he''s in the photo. He adds a lot of interest to an already super interesting spot. The exposure is perfect.</td>', 'Very pretty lighting... so golden! I would love to visit Jordan someday. You''ve shown me such a beautiful place. Might be nice to see the boy in front of one of the pillars so he stands out a little more, but I''m really glad he''s in the photo. He adds a lot of interest to an already super interesting spot. The exposure is perfect.', '2006-11-29 04:46:34.000000', NULL, 0),
